# Model Routing Workflow

The Sol High parent leads ordinary repository inspection, planning, acceptance
criteria, integrated-diff review, and final signoff. It may directly implement
hard work when appropriate.

This is the original Sol/Terra/Luna Cursor workflow. Do not use `composer-owner`,
`grok-advisor`, `grok-architect`, `grok-reviewer`, or `grok-escalation` here;
those agents are reserved for sessions launched with `cursor-st --groky`.

## Non-Fast invariant

Every managed model in this hierarchy must run with `fast=false`.

- Sol High parent: `gpt-5.6-sol` + high reasoning, launcher-enforced `fast=false`.
- Sol Max advisor: `gpt-5.6-sol-max[fast=false]`.
- Terra implementer: `gpt-5.6-terra-medium[fast=false]`.
- Terra reviewer: `gpt-5.6-terra-high[fast=false]`.
- Luna worker: `gpt-5.6-luna-medium[fast=false]`.

Do not switch Fast on to reduce latency. Prefer direct parent tools or the pinned custom agents over unspecified/built-in subagents whose speed variant cannot be verified.

## Classify the task

A bounded Luna task is low-risk only when all of the following are true:

- The intended change is obvious
- It is localized and low-risk
- It does not alter architecture, APIs, persistence, authentication,
  concurrency, security boundaries, or core behavior
- Acceptance can be verified with a focused command or inspection

Luna handles only explicit bounded repository search, boilerplate, docs,
fixtures/mocks/schemas, established-pattern basic components, mechanical
changes, repetitive tests/checks, formatting, and reporting.

Terra Medium is the default primary implementer for roughly 70–80% of ordinary
implementation, tests, routine debugging, APIs, components, CLIs, backend
logic, and integration. This is a routing target, not a quota.

## Canonical workflow

1. Sol High inspects the repository, plans, and defines acceptance criteria.
2. Terra implements core work and tests.
3. Luna provides only explicit bounded support.
4. Terra integrates and performs routine/advisory review, especially for Luna work.
5. Sol High reviews the complete integrated diff and alone gives final signoff.

Do not run agents concurrently when their write scopes overlap.

## Sol Max escalation advisor

`sol-planner` is a read-only Sol Max advisor, not a mandatory stage. Invoke it
only for architecture or security risk, unusually difficult reasoning, stalled
debugging, or a fundamental review finding. It may return `[SOL]`, `[TERRA]`,
and `[LUNA]` ownership guidance to the Sol High parent.

Do not use Sol Max for routine coding, test execution, formatting,
documentation, simple debugging, or ordinary review.

## Completion gate

Do not claim completion until:

- Required implementation exists
- Relevant verification has run
- Test results are reported honestly
- Terra routine-review findings are addressed or explicitly documented
- Sol High has reviewed the complete integrated diff and given final signoff
- Remaining limitations are explicitly documented
